        }
      ],
      "message": "fix(wallet): avoid crash if db create fails in migration\n\nMigrateToSQLite() deleted the legacy BDB file before creating the new\nSQLite database, then asserted that the creation succeeded.  When\nit fails, for example because the wallet directory is on a network\nfilesystem (SMB/CIFS) where SQLite cannot obtain an exclusive lock,\nor the filesystem is full or has permission errors, the node aborts\nwith \"Assertion `new_db' failed\" and the wallet file is gone, leaving\nonly the .legacy.bak backup made before migration.\n\nCreate the new database next to the old one, and swap it in only\nafter the creation is successful.\n\nIf the new database fails before completing, remove the failed\nattempt and return an error with the underlying reason and a hint.\n\nThe legacy file is deleted once all records have been committed to\nthe new database and it's in place.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "David R. Hedges",
        "email": "bitcoindev651@thelittleman.net",
        "date": "2026-11-09T18:58:00Z"
      },
